#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:9
msgid "Reimplementing ifconfig in Python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:11
msgid ""
"Here we are. It's been a long time since my last blog post and my last "
"psutil release. The reason? I've been travelling! I mean... a lot. I've "
"spent 3 months in Berlin, 3 weeks in Japan and 2 months in New York City. "
"While I was there I finally had the chance to meet my friend `Jay Loden "
"<http://jayloden.com/software.htm>`__ in person. We originally started "
"working on psutil together `7 years ago <https://groups.google.com/forum/#!"
"topic/psutil-dev/fj8DQ3lGFH4>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:19
msgid "Jay and I"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:24
msgid ""
"Back then I didn't know any C (and I'm still a terrible C developer), so he "
"was crucial in developing the initial psutil skeleton, including macOS and "
"Windows support. Needless to say that this release builds on that work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:29
msgid "net_if_addrs()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:31
msgid ""
"We're now able to list network interface addresses similarly to the "
"``ifconfig`` command on UNIX:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:34
msgid ""
">>> import psutil\n"
">>> from pprint import pprint\n"
">>> pprint(psutil.net_if_addrs())\n"
"{'ethernet0': [snic(family=<AddressFamily.AF_INET: 2>,\n"
"                    address='10.0.0.4',\n"
"                    netmask='255.0.0.0',\n"
"                    broadcast='10.255.255.255'),\n"
"               snic(family=<AddressFamily.AF_PACKET: 17>,\n"
"                    address='9c:eb:e8:0b:05:1f',\n"
"                    netmask=None,\n"
"                    broadcast='ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff')],\n"
" 'localhost': [snic(family=<AddressFamily.AF_INET: 2>,\n"
"                    address='127.0.0.1',\n"
"                    netmask='255.0.0.0',\n"
"                    broadcast='127.0.0.1'),\n"
"               snic(family=<AddressFamily.AF_PACKET: 17>,\n"
"                    address='00:00:00:00:00:00',\n"
"                    netmask=None,\n"
"                    broadcast='00:00:00:00:00:00')]}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:56
msgid ""
"This is limited to ``AF_INET`` (IPv4), ``AF_INET6`` (IPv6) and ``AF_LINK`` "
"(Ethernet) address families. If you want something more powerful (e.g. "
"``AF_BLUETOOTH``) you can take a look at the `netifaces <https://pypi.python."
"org/pypi/netifaces/>`__ extension. If you want to see how this is "
"implemented, here's the code for POSIX and Windows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:62
msgid ""
"`POSIX <https://github.com/giampaolo/psutil/"
"blob/39161251010503d6b087807c473f4fb648dfcbce/psutil/_psutil_posix.c#L151>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:63
msgid ""
"`Windows <https://github.com/giampaolo/psutil/"
"blob/39161251010503d6b087807c473f4fb648dfcbce/psutil/_psutil_windows."
"c#L2907>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:66
msgid "net_if_stats()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:68
msgid "This new function returns information about network interface cards:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:70
msgid ""
">>> import psutil\n"
">>> from pprint import pprint\n"
">>> pprint(psutil.net_if_stats())\n"
"{'ethernet0': snicstats(isup=True,\n"
"                        duplex=<NicDuplex.NIC_DUPLEX_FULL: 2>,\n"
"                        speed=100,\n"
"                        mtu=1500),\n"
" 'localhost': snicstats(isup=True,\n"
"                        duplex=<NicDuplex.NIC_DUPLEX_UNKNOWN: 0>,\n"
"                        speed=0,\n"
"                        mtu=65536)}"
msgstr ""

