#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:92
msgid "Also in 3.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:94
msgid ""
"Beyond the network-interface APIs, psutil 3.0 ships a few other notable "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:97
msgid ""
"Several integer/string constants (``IOPRIO_CLASS_*``, ``NIC_DUPLEX_*``, "
"``*_PRIORITY_CLASS``) now return :mod:`enum` values on Python 3.4+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:100
msgid ""
"Support for :term:`zombie processes <zombie process>` on UNIX was broken. "
"Covered in a :doc:`separate post </blog/2015/zombie-processes>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:103
msgid ""
"All aliases deprecated in the :doc:`psutil 2.0 porting guide </blog/2014/"
"porting-to-20>` (January 2014) are gone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:107
msgid "For a full list of changes see the :ref:`changelog <300>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:110
msgid "Final words"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:112
msgid ""
"I must say I'm pretty satisfied with how psutil is evolving and with the "
"enjoyment I still get every time I work on it. It now gets almost `800,000 "
"downloads a month <https://pypi.org/project/psutil/>`__, which is quite "
"remarkable for a Python library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:117
msgid ""
"At this point, I consider psutil almost \"complete\" feature-wise, meaning "
"I'm starting to run out of ideas for what to add next (see `TODO <https://"
"github.com/giampaolo/psutil/blob/v3.0.0/TODO>`__). Going forward, "
"development will likely focus on supporting more exotic platforms (OpenBSD :"
"gh:`562`, NetBSD :pr:`557`, Android :gh:`355`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2015/reimplementing-ifconfig-in-python.rst:123
msgid ""
"There have also been discussions on the python-ideas mailing list about "
"`including psutil in the Python stdlib <https://mail.python.org/pipermail//"
"python-ideas/2014-October/029835.html>`__, but even if that happens, it's "
"still a long way off, as it would require a significant time investment that "
"I currently don't have."
msgstr ""
